The administration also reminds that tsunamis can produce multiple waves; after the first wave, people should remain in safe locations until a “tsunami alert lifted” or “tsunami warning lifted” notice is issued before returning to coastal areas.

The PTWC warned that areas within 620 miles (998 km) of the epicenter—including the Cayman Islands, Jamaica, Cuba, Mexico, Honduras, the Bahamas, Belize, Haiti, Costa Rica, Panama, Nicaragua and Guatemala—should remain alert.
